    "title": "2 pulled from submerged vehicle in Waukee pond have died - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Natasha Keicher ,\n8 hours ago\nWAUKEE, Iowa — Two people who were pulled from a submerged vehicle in a Waukee pond have died.\nMeasles case confirmed in Polk County On Tuesday afternoon, the Waukee Police Department responded to a report of a vehicle that had crashed into a pond on Manchester Boulevard/NW Stratford Drive. Two people were pulled from the vehicle and transported to a local hospital.\nThe WPD announced on Wednesday that the two occupants had died. They have been identified as 43-year-old Titus Wanjala and 23-year-old River Cropper.\nAn investigation into the crash is ongoing. No additional information has been released.\nMetro news Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to who13.com.\n8",
